  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Immediate damage reconstruction and sustainable solutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at restoring access to quality drinking water and water treatment services for citizens in four territorial communities in an area heavily affected by war.Project partners will make immediate repairs to the water system by buying and installing equipment like, among others, pumps and pipes. Furthermore, the regional administration and territorial administrations will be supported by the project partners in the development of an &apos;integrated water resources management vision&apos;. Part of this vision are trainings on the maintenance of the equipment and coaching local government in further restoring and professionalising the collection of user fees. By doing so, the partners have ensured that the project will have impact after the completion date.When the project is completed, it will result in improved water treatment services and reliable access to water will be restored for approximately 10,000 households, as well as to a number of schools, medical facilities and companies.</narrative>
  </description>
